const e={id:"mongo-insert-find",title:{en:"Insert & Find: Comparison & Logical Operators",hi:"Insert & Find: Operators ($gt, $in, $and, $or)"},difficulty:"Beginner",readTime:10,sections:[{type:"concept",heading:{en:"1. MongoDB Query Fundamentals: Insert & Find",hi:"1. MongoDB Query Fundamentals: Insert aur Find"},body:{en:"MongoDB stores data as BSON documents inside collections. The primary operations for adding and querying data are:\n\n### Insertion Methods:\n- `insertOne(doc, options)`: Inserts a single document. If no `_id` field is provided, MongoDB automatically generates a 12-byte `ObjectId`.\n- `insertMany([doc1, doc2, ...], options)`: Inserts an array of documents atomically in batches. By default, it operates with `{ ordered: true }` (if document 3 fails validation, operations stop immediately). With `{ ordered: false }`, execution continues for subsequent valid documents.\n\n### Query Methods:\n- `findOne(filter, projection)`: Returns the **first matching document** as a plain JavaScript object, or `null` if nothing matches.\n- `find(filter, projection)`: Returns an active **MongoDB Cursor** (an iterable pointer) to documents matching the criteria. Does not load all documents into Node.js memory at once!",hi:"MongoDB mein data BSON documents ke roop mein collections ke andar store hota hai. Data create aur fetch karne ke mukhya functions yeh hain:\n\n### Insert Karne Ke Methods:\n- `insertOne(doc, options)`: Ek single document insert karta hai. Agar aap `_id` provide nahi karte, toh MongoDB automatically ek unique 12-byte `ObjectId` generate kar deta hai.\n- `insertMany([doc1, doc2, ...], options)`: Documents ki array ko batch mein insert karta hai. By default `{ ordered: true }` hota hai (agar 3rd document fail ho jaye toh aage ke inserts ruk jaate hain). `{ ordered: false }` se baaki valid documents insert hote rehte hain.\n\n### Query Karne Ke Methods:\n- `findOne(filter, projection)`: Filter match karne wala **pehla document** return karta hai, ya koi match na mile toh `null` deta hai.\n- `find(filter, projection)`: Matches par ek **Cursor** (iterable pointer) return karta hai. Yeh saare documents ko ek sath RAM mein load nahi karta, balki chunks mein stream karta hai!"}},{type:"concept",heading:{en:"2. Comparison & Logical Operators",hi:"2. Comparison aur Logical Operators Ka Khel"},body:{en:"In SQL, you write `WHERE price > 500 AND category = 'Electronics'`. In MongoDB, all queries are expressed as JSON/BSON filter objects using special `$` prefixed operator keys.\n\n### Comparison Operators:\n- `$eq`: Equal to (`{ age: { $eq: 25 } }` or shorthand `{ age: 25 }`)\n- `$ne`: Not equal to (`{ status: { $ne: 'deleted' } }`)\n- `$gt` / `$gte`: Greater than / Greater than or equal to (`{ price: { $gte: 999 } }`)\n- `$lt` / `$lte`: Less than / Less than or equal to (`{ rating: { $lt: 3.5 } }`)\n- `$in`: Matches any value in an array (`{ category: { $in: ['Mobiles', 'Laptops'] } }`)\n- `$nin`: Not in array (`{ role: { $nin: ['banned', 'suspended'] } }`)\n\n### Logical Operators:\n- `$and`: Joins query clauses where **all** conditions must match (`{ $and: [{ inStock: true }, { price: { $lt: 500 } }] }`)\n- `$or`: Joins query clauses where **at least one** condition must match (`{ $or: [{ role: 'admin' }, { isSuperUser: true }] }`)\n- `$nor`: Fails if any of the given clauses match\n- `$not`: Inverts the effect of a query expression (`{ price: { $not: { $gt: 100 } } }`)",hi:"SQL mein aap likhte the `WHERE price > 500 AND category = 'Electronics'`. MongoDB mein saari queries JSON object ke form mein hoti hain jahan operators `$` sign se shuru hote hain.\n\n### Comparison Operators:\n- `$eq`: Barabar (equal) (`{ age: { $eq: 25 } }` ya simple `{ age: 25 }`)\n- `$ne`: Barabar nahi (not equal) (`{ status: { $ne: 'deleted' } }`)\n- `$gt` / `$gte`: Bada / Bada ya barabar (`{ price: { $gte: 999 } }`)\n- `$lt` / `$lte`: Chhota / Chhota ya barabar (`{ rating: { $lt: 3.5 } }`)\n- `$in`: Array ke kisi bhi ek value se match kare (`{ city: { $in: ['Delhi', 'Mumbai', 'Bangalore'] } }`)\n- `$nin`: Array ke kisi bhi value se match na kare (`{ role: { $nin: ['blocked', 'deleted'] } }`)\n\n### Logical Operators:\n- `$and`: Saari shartein poori honi chahiye (`{ $and: [{ inStock: true }, { price: { $lt: 500 } }] }`)\n- `$or`: Di gayi sharton mein se kam se kam ek sahi ho (`{ $or: [{ role: 'admin' }, { isSuperUser: true }] }`)\n- `$nor`: Di gayi koi bhi shart match nahi honi chahiye\n- `$not`: Kisi query expression ko ulta karta hai"}},{type:"analogy",heading:{en:"Real-Life Analogy: The Kirana Store Grocery Register",hi:"Real-Life Analogy: Desi Kirana Store Ka Udhar & Stock Register"},body:{en:"Imagine Sharma-ji managing his neighborhood grocery store (Kirana store) with a master inventory notebook:\n\n- **`insertOne`**: Sharma-ji writes down a brand new sack of Basmati Rice arrived today on line 42 with its purchase date and cost price.\n- **`insertMany`**: The wholesale milk distributor delivers Amul Milk, Paneer, Curd, and Butter at 6:00 AM. Sharma-ji records all 4 dairy items together in one quick batch entry.\n- **`findOne({ item: 'Tata Salt' })`**: A customer asks \"Do you have Tata Salt?\". Sharma-ji looks down at his register, finds the first packet on shelf 2, and answers immediately.\n- **`find({ price: { $lte: 50 }, category: 'Biscuits' })`**: A kid enters with a ₹50 note saying \"Bhaiya, show me all biscuits under ₹50!\". Sharma-ji checks Parle-G (₹10), Good Day (₹30), and Bourbon (₹40).\n- **`{ brand: { $in: ['Amul', 'Mother Dairy'] } }`**: A customer wants butter only from Amul or Mother Dairy, ignoring other local brands.",hi:"Sochiye Sharma-ji apne mohalle ke Kirana Store mein ek notebook maintain kar rahe hain:\n\n- **`insertOne`**: Subah ek naya dry-fruits ka box aaya. Sharma-ji ne register ki line 42 par uska naam, expiry date aur price likh diya.\n- **`insertMany`**: Subah 6 baje Amul ki gaadi aayi aur doodh, dahi, paneer, aur butter deliver kiya. Sharma-ji ne ek sath 4 items register mein note kar liye.\n- **`findOne({ item: 'Tata Salt' })`**: Grahak ne poocha \"Tata Salt hai kya?\". Sharma-ji ne register dekha aur pehla packet utha kar de diya.\n- **`find({ price: { $lte: 50 }, category: 'Biscuits' })`**: Ek bachha ₹50 ka note laya aur bola \"50 rupaye ke andar waale saare biscuits dikhao!\". Sharma-ji ne filter lagaya: Parle-G (₹10), Marie Gold (₹30), Bourbon (₹40).\n- **`{ brand: { $in: ['Amul', 'Mother Dairy'] } }`**: Grahak ne bola mujhe sirf Amul ya Mother Dairy ka dahi chahiye, baaki koi local brand nahi."}},{type:"syntax",heading:{en:"Syntax & Signature: Native Driver vs Mongoose",hi:"Syntax & Signatures: Native MongoDB Driver aur Mongoose"},body:{en:`### Native MongoDB Driver Syntax:
\`\`\`javascript
// Insert operations
const result = await collection.insertOne({ name: "Aman", age: 24 });
console.log(result.insertedId); // ObjectId("...")

const batchResult = await collection.insertMany([
  { name: "Pooja", age: 22 },
  { name: "Rohan", age: 28 }
], { ordered: true });
console.log(batchResult.insertedCount); // 2

// Find operations
const singleUser = await collection.findOne({ email: "aman@example.com" });

// Find returns a Cursor - convert to Array or iterate
const adultUsers = await collection.find({
  age: { $gte: 18 },
  city: { $in: ["Delhi", "Mumbai"] }
}).toArray();
\`\`\`

### Mongoose Query Shorthand:
\`\`\`javascript
// In Mongoose, find() returns a Query (thenable)
const users = await User.find({
  price: { $gte: 500, $lte: 2000 },
  tags: { $in: ["electronics", "gadgets"] }
});
\`\`\``,hi:`### Native MongoDB Driver Syntax:
\`\`\`javascript
// Insert operation
const result = await collection.insertOne({ name: "Aman", age: 24 });
console.log(result.insertedId); // Generated ObjectId

// Insert many
const batchResult = await collection.insertMany([
  { name: "Pooja", age: 22 },
  { name: "Rohan", age: 28 }
]);

// Find single document
const user = await collection.findOne({ email: "aman@example.com" });

// Find returns Cursor -> .toArray() use karein array lene ke liye
const activeUsers = await collection.find({
  age: { $gte: 18 },
  status: "active"
}).toArray();
\`\`\``}},{type:"example",heading:{en:"Example 1: Basic Inserts and Simple Comparisons",hi:"Example 1: Basic Inserts aur Simple Comparisons"},body:{en:"Inserting documents into a `students` collection and querying with numeric boundary comparisons (`$gt`, `$lte`).",hi:"`students` collection mein documents insert karna aur numeric operators se search karna."},code:{language:"javascript",filename:"basic-insert-find.js",snippet:`import { MongoClient } from "mongodb";

const uri = "mongodb://127.0.0.1:27017";
const client = new MongoClient(uri);

async function run() {
  try {
    await client.connect();
    const db = client.db("schoolDB");
    const students = db.collection("students");

    // Clean previous test data
    await students.deleteMany({});

    // 1. insertMany
    const insertResult = await students.insertMany([
      { name: "Aarav Sharma", score: 92, stream: "Science", passed: true },
      { name: "Diya Patel", score: 78, stream: "Commerce", passed: true },
      { name: "Kabir Verma", score: 45, stream: "Arts", passed: false },
      { name: "Ananya Iyer", score: 88, stream: "Science", passed: true },
      { name: "Vikram Singh", score: 55, stream: "Commerce", passed: true }
    ]);
    console.log(\`Inserted \${insertResult.insertedCount} students.\`);

    // 2. Query students with score >= 75 (Distinction)
    const toppers = await students.find({
      score: { $gte: 75 }
    }).toArray();
    console.log("Toppers (score >= 75):", toppers.map(s => \`\${s.name} (\${s.score})\`));

    // 3. Query science students who scored strictly less than 90
    const scienceUnder90 = await students.find({
      stream: "Science",
      score: { $lt: 90 }
    }).toArray();
    console.log("Science students < 90:", scienceUnder90.map(s => s.name));

  } finally {
    await client.close();
  }
}

run().catch(console.error);

/*
Expected Output:
Inserted 5 students.
Toppers (score >= 75): [ 'Aarav Sharma (92)', 'Diya Patel (78)', 'Ananya Iyer (88)' ]
Science students < 90: [ 'Ananya Iyer' ]
*/`}},{type:"example",heading:{en:"Example 2: Complex Logical Queries ($or, $and, $in, $regex)",hi:"Example 2: Logical Queries ($or, $and, $in, $regex)"},body:{en:"Executing sophisticated multi-clause queries using `$or`, `$in` array memberships, and case-insensitive regex filtering.",hi:"`$or`, `$in` aur regex search ke sath multi-condition queries execute karna."},code:{language:"javascript",filename:"logical-operators.js",snippet:`import { MongoClient } from "mongodb";

const client = new MongoClient("mongodb://127.0.0.1:27017");

async function filterUsers() {
  await client.connect();
  const users = client.db("appDB").collection("users");

  await users.deleteMany({});
  await users.insertMany([
    { name: "Rajesh Kumar", role: "moderator", city: "Jaipur", karma: 420 },
    { name: "Neha Gupta", role: "admin", city: "Bengaluru", karma: 1200 },
    { name: "Sunil Joshi", role: "user", city: "Mumbai", karma: 150 },
    { name: "Priya Menon", role: "user", city: "Chennai", karma: 890 },
    { name: "Amitabh Roy", role: "moderator", city: "Kolkata", karma: 50 }
  ]);

  // Query: Users who are EITHER 'admin' OR have karma >= 800
  // AND reside in either Bengaluru, Mumbai, or Chennai
  const privilegedOrHighKarmaInMetros = await users.find({
    $and: [
      {
        $or: [
          { role: "admin" },
          { karma: { $gte: 800 } }
        ]
      },
      {
        city: { $in: ["Bengaluru", "Mumbai", "Chennai"] }
      }
    ]
  }).toArray();

  console.log("Matched Users:", privilegedOrHighKarmaInMetros.map(u => ({
    name: u.name,
    role: u.role,
    karma: u.karma,
    city: u.city
  })));

  // Regex Query: Search users whose name contains 'kumar' or 'gupta' (case-insensitive)
  const patternMatch = await users.find({
    name: { $regex: /kumar|gupta/i }
  }).toArray();
  console.log("Regex Name Search:", patternMatch.map(u => u.name));

  await client.close();
}

filterUsers().catch(console.error);

/*
Expected Output:
Matched Users: [
  { name: 'Neha Gupta', role: 'admin', karma: 1200, city: 'Bengaluru' },
  { name: 'Priya Menon', role: 'user', karma: 890, city: 'Chennai' }
]
Regex Name Search: [ 'Rajesh Kumar', 'Neha Gupta' ]
*/`}},{type:"example",heading:{en:"Example 3: Real-World E-Commerce Product Catalog Filter Service",hi:"Example 3: Production E-Commerce Product Filter Service"},body:{en:"A production-ready query builder function handling dynamic query params (price range, brands array, in-stock toggle, text search).",hi:"Production-ready dynamic product filter service jo Express API ke query parameters ko MongoDB queries mein translate karti hai."},code:{language:"javascript",filename:"product-filter-service.js",snippet:`/**
 * Builds a dynamic MongoDB filter object from incoming HTTP req.query
 * Handles price ranges, array matching, text search, and stock status.
 */
export function buildProductFilter(queryParams) {
  const filter = { isDeleted: { $ne: true } };

  // 1. Text search across title & description
  if (queryParams.search) {
    // Sanitize regex special characters
    const escaped = queryParams.search.replace(/[.*+?^\${}()|[\\]\\\\]/g, "\\\\$&");
    filter.title = { $regex: escaped, $options: "i" };
  }

  // 2. Numeric Price Range Filter ($gte, $lte)
  if (queryParams.minPrice || queryParams.maxPrice) {
    filter.price = {};
    if (queryParams.minPrice) filter.price.$gte = Number(queryParams.minPrice);
    if (queryParams.maxPrice) filter.price.$lte = Number(queryParams.maxPrice);
  }

  // 3. Multi-brand selection ($in)
  if (queryParams.brands) {
    const brandList = Array.isArray(queryParams.brands)
      ? queryParams.brands
      : queryParams.brands.split(",");
    filter.brand = { $in: brandList.map(b => b.trim()) };
  }

  // 4. In-stock Boolean filter ($gt on quantity)
  if (queryParams.inStock === "true" || queryParams.inStock === true) {
    filter.stockQuantity = { $gt: 0 };
  }

  // 5. Customer Rating threshold
  if (queryParams.minRating) {
    filter.rating = { $gte: Number(queryParams.minRating) };
  }

  return filter;
}

// Simulation Test
const incomingRequestQuery = {
  search: "wireless earphone",
  minPrice: "1000",
  maxPrice: "4000",
  brands: "Boat,Noise,Realme",
  inStock: "true",
  minRating: "4.0"
};

const mongoFilter = buildProductFilter(incomingRequestQuery);
console.log("Generated MongoDB Filter Object:");
console.log(JSON.stringify(mongoFilter, null, 2));

/*
Expected Output:
Generated MongoDB Filter Object:
{
  "isDeleted": { "$ne": true },
  "title": { "$regex": "wireless earphone", "$options": "i" },
  "price": { "$gte": 1000, "$lte": 4000 },
  "brand": { "$in": ["Boat", "Noise", "Realme"] },
  "stockQuantity": { "$gt": 0 },
  "rating": { "$gte": 4 }
}
*/`}},{type:"mistakes",heading:{en:"Common Mistakes & How to Fix Them",hi:"Aam Galatiyan Aur Unka Solution"},body:{en:"### 1. Passing a Plain String Instead of `new ObjectId(id)` in Native Driver\n- **Mistake**: Calling `collection.findOne({ _id: \"655b12f8a...\" })`. In native MongoDB driver, `_id` is stored as a BSON `ObjectId` binary type. A string will return `null`!\n- **Fix**: Always convert hex strings: `import { ObjectId } from 'mongodb'; collection.findOne({ _id: new ObjectId(id) })`. (Note: Mongoose casts automatically, but the native driver does not).\n\n### 2. Overwriting Duplicate Keys in JavaScript Objects\n- **Mistake**: Writing `{ price: { $gt: 100 }, price: { $lt: 500 } }`. In JavaScript, the second `price` key overwrites the first! Only `price: { $lt: 500 }` executes.\n- **Fix**: Combine them into one operator object: `{ price: { $gt: 100, $lt: 500 } }` or use `$and`.\n\n### 3. Using JavaScript Array `[...]` Instead of `$in`\n- **Mistake**: Writing `{ category: ['Electronics', 'Books'] }`. This looks for documents where `category` is literally an array containing both items in that exact order!\n- **Fix**: Use `{ category: { $in: ['Electronics', 'Books'] } }` to match any document belonging to either category.\n\n### 4. Forgetting to Await `toArray()` on `find()`\n- **Mistake**: `const users = collection.find({ active: true });` — `users` is a Cursor object, not an array of documents!\n- **Fix**: Always call and await: `const users = await collection.find({ active: true }).toArray();`.",hi:"### 1. Native Driver Mein String ID Pass Karna\n- **Galati**: `collection.findOne({ _id: \"655b12f8a...\" })` likhna. Native driver mein `_id` BSON `ObjectId` hota hai, raw string dhoondne par hamesha `null` milega!\n- **Solution**: `new ObjectId(id)` mein convert karein: `collection.findOne({ _id: new ObjectId(id) })`.\n\n### 2. JavaScript Object Mein Duplicate Keys Overwrite Hona\n- **Galati**: `{ price: { $gt: 100 }, price: { $lt: 500 } }` likhna. JavaScript doosre `price` se pehle wale ko mita deta hai!\n- **Solution**: Dono operators ek hi object mein rakhein: `{ price: { $gt: 100, $lt: 500 } }`.\n\n### 3. Array Equality vs `$in` Operator\n- **Galati**: `{ category: ['Mobile', 'Laptop'] }` likhna. Isse wahi document match honge jinki category exact yeh array hogi.\n- **Solution**: Agar dono mein se koi bhi match chahiye toh `$in` use karein: `{ category: { $in: ['Mobile', 'Laptop'] } }`.\n\n### 4. `find()` Par `toArray()` Na Lagana\n- **Galati**: `const users = collection.find({ active: true })` likhna. Yeh Cursor object deta hai, data array nahi.\n- **Solution**: `await collection.find(...).toArray()` use karein."}},{type:"tip",heading:{en:"Best Practices for Insert & Find Operations",hi:"Insert & Find Ke Best Practices"},body:{en:"1. **Prefer `$in` Over Multiple `$or` Clauses**: `{ status: { $in: ['pending', 'failed'] } }` is dramatically faster and easier for the query planner to index than `{ $or: [{ status: 'pending' }, { status: 'failed' }] }`.\n2. **Never Perform Unbounded `find()`**: Always combine `find()` with `.limit()` or pagination to prevent bringing 500,000 documents into Node.js heap memory and crashing the server (OOM error).\n3. **Use `insertMany` with `{ ordered: false }` for Bulk Imports**: If you are importing 10,000 records, unordered insertion lets MongoDB process writes concurrently across shards and won't halt on a single duplicate key error.\n4. **Always Sanitize User Inputs in `$regex` Queries**: Avoid ReDoS (Regular Expression Denial of Service) by escaping user query strings or prefer text indexes (`$text`).",hi:"1. **Multiple `$or` Ki Jagah `$in` Use Karein**: `{ status: { $in: ['pending', 'failed'] } }` MongoDB ke query optimizer ke liye fast hota hai.\n2. **Khabhi Bhi Unbounded `find()` Na Chalayein**: Hamesha `.limit()` ya pagination lagayein, warna lakhon records Node.js ki memory mein aakar server crash (Out Of Memory) kar denge.\n3. **Bulk Data Ke Liye `{ ordered: false }` Use Karein**: 10,000 records import karte waqt `ordered: false` se ek duplicate error ki wajah se poora batch nahi rukta.\n4. **User Input Regex Ko Escape Karein**: ReDoS attack se bachne ke liye user input ko hamesha sanitize karein ya Full-Text Search (`$text`) ka use karein."}},{type:"interview",heading:{en:"Top Interview Questions & Answers",hi:"Top Interview Sawaal Aur Jawab"},body:{en:'### Q1: What is the difference between `findOne()` and `find()`?\n**Answer**:\n- `findOne(filter)`: Returns a single plain JavaScript document directly from disk into memory. If no document matches, it resolves to `null`.\n- `find(filter)`: Does **not** return documents directly. It returns an active **MongoDB Cursor**. The cursor fetches records in batches (default batch size ~101 documents or 4 MB) as you iterate or call `.toArray()`.\n\n### Q2: What happens when `insertMany()` encounters an error halfway through with `ordered: true` vs `ordered: false`?\n**Answer**:\n- `ordered: true` (default): Documents are inserted serially in array order. If document index 4 violates a unique index, insertion stops immediately. Documents 0 to 3 remain inserted, but documents 5 and beyond are never attempted.\n- `ordered: false`: MongoDB attempts to insert all documents in parallel. If document 4 fails, it records the write error in the bulk response, but documents 5, 6, and onwards are still processed and inserted.\n\n### Q3: How do `$and` and implicit comma separation differ in MongoDB queries?\n**Answer**:\n`{ age: { $gte: 18 }, status: "active" }` implicitly applies an AND condition between different fields. You only need explicit `$and` when you need to query the **same field multiple times** with different conditions (like `{ $and: [{ tags: "tech" }, { tags: "news" }] }`) or combine multiple `$or` blocks.',hi:'### Q1: `findOne()` aur `find()` mein kya antar hai?\n**Jawab**:\n- `findOne(filter)`: Filter match karne wala single document seedhe memory mein lata hai. Match na milne par `null` deta hai.\n- `find(filter)`: Documents seedhe nahi deta, balki ek **Cursor** return karta hai jo background mein 101 documents ya 4 MB ke batches mein stream karta hai.\n\n### Q2: `insertMany` mein `ordered: true` aur `ordered: false` mein kya farq hai?\n**Jawab**:\n- `ordered: true` (default): Serial execution hota hai. Agar 4th document par unique key error aaya toh operation wahin ruk jata hai; 5th document insert nahi hoga.\n- `ordered: false`: Parallel execution hota hai. 4th document fail hone par bhi aage ke saare valid documents insert ho jate hain aur end mein errors ki list milti hai.\n\n### Q3: Implicit AND aur explicit `$and` operator mein kya antar hai?\n**Jawab**:\n`{ age: { $gte: 18 }, status: "active" }` comma laga kar likhne par internally AND hi hota hai. Explicit `$and` ki zaroorat tab padti hai jab aapko ek hi field par alag-alag expressions chalane hon ya do `$or` conditions ko aapas mein jodhna ho.'}},{type:"summary",heading:{en:"Quick Summary: Insert & Find Operators",hi:"Quick Summary: Insert & Find Operators"},body:{en:"- **`insertOne` & `insertMany`**: Primary insertion methods; `ordered: false` enables unordered bulk insertion.\n- **`find` returns a Cursor**: Never forgets that `find()` streams data; consume with `.toArray()` or a `for await...of` loop.\n- **Comparison Operators**: `$eq`, `$ne`, `$gt`, `$gte`, `$lt`, `$lte`, `$in`, `$nin`.\n- **Logical Operators**: `$and`, `$or`, `$nor`, `$not` for compound conditional logic.\n- **Array matching**: Use `$in` to check if a field matches any value in a list of allowed choices.",hi:"- **`insertOne` aur `insertMany`**: Data create karne ke methods; `ordered: false` se fast batch inserts hote hain.\n- **`find` Cursor return karta hai**: Lakhon records se memory bachane ke liye cursor ka use hota hai, `.toArray()` se array milti hai.\n- **Comparison Operators**: `$gt`, `$gte`, `$lt`, `$lte`, `$in` value compare karte hain.\n- **Logical Operators**: `$and`, `$or`, `$not` conditions ko jodne ke kaam aate hain.\n- **`$in` Best Practice**: Multiple `$or` conditions se behtar aur tez `$in` operator hota hai."}}],quiz:[{q:{en:"What does collection.find({ age: { $gt: 20 } }) return in the native Node.js MongoDB driver?",hi:"Native Node.js MongoDB driver mein collection.find(...) kya return karta hai?"},options:[{en:"An array of all matched documents in memory",hi:"Memory mein saare matched documents ka array"},{en:"A MongoDB Cursor pointing to the query results",hi:"Query results ki taraf point karne wala MongoDB Cursor"},{en:"A single matched document object",hi:"Ek single matched document object"},{en:"A boolean indicating if matching records exist",hi:"Ek boolean jo batata hai ki record mila ya nahi"}],answerIndex:1,explanation:{en:"find() returns a Cursor stream. You must call .toArray() or iterate with a cursor loop to retrieve the actual document records.",hi:"find() Cursor return karta hai. Documents pane ke liye .toArray() ya cursor iteration ka use karna padta hai."}},{q:{en:"Which operator matches documents where a field value equals ANY value in a provided list?",hi:"Kaunsa operator un documents ko dhoondta hai jinki value di gayi list mein se kisi bhi ek value se match kare?"},options:[{en:"$all",hi:"$all"},{en:"$in",hi:"$in"},{en:"$or",hi:"$or"},{en:"$eqArray",hi:"$eqArray"}],answerIndex:1,explanation:{en:"$in takes an array of values and matches documents where the field equals any member of that array.",hi:"$in ek array leta hai aur un sabhi documents ko match karta hai jahan field value us array ke kisi bhi element ke barabar ho."}},{q:{en:"Why is { price: { $gt: 100 }, price: { $lt: 500 } } buggy in plain JavaScript?",hi:"Plain JavaScript mein { price: { $gt: 100 }, price: { $lt: 500 } } mein kya bug hai?"},options:[{en:"MongoDB doesn't support $gt and $lt together",hi:"MongoDB $gt aur $lt ek sath support nahi karta"},{en:"JavaScript object duplicate keys overwrite earlier ones, losing $gt: 100",hi:"JavaScript object mein duplicate keys pehle wali key ko overwrite kar deti hain"},{en:"Prices must always be integers in MongoDB",hi:"MongoDB mein price hamesha integer hona chahiye"},{en:"The query requires an explicit $between operator",hi:"Query ke liye explicit $between operator chahiye"}],answerIndex:1,explanation:{en:"In standard JS object syntax, duplicate keys overwrite previous ones. You must write { price: { $gt: 100, $lt: 500 } }.",hi:"JavaScript objects mein same key do baar likhne par baad wali key pehli wali ko overwrite kar deti hai."}},{q:{en:"What is the behavior of insertMany([...], { ordered: false }) if document index 2 causes a duplicate key error?",hi:"insertMany([...], { ordered: false }) mein agar 2nd document duplicate error de, toh kya hoga?"},options:[{en:"All inserted documents are rolled back completely",hi:"Saare inserted documents rollback ho jayenge"},{en:"Execution halts and subsequent documents are skipped",hi:"Execution ruk jayegi aur aage ke documents skip ho jayenge"},{en:"Error is logged, but remaining valid documents are still inserted",hi:"Error log hoga, lekin baaki valid documents insert ho jayenge"},{en:"The duplicate document overwrites the existing record",hi:"Duplicate document purane record ko overwrite kar dega"}],answerIndex:2,explanation:{en:"With { ordered: false }, MongoDB continues inserting all remaining valid documents in the array even if one fails.",hi:"ordered: false ke sath kisi ek document ke fail hone par bhi baaki sabhi valid documents insert hote rehte hain."}},{question:{en:"What is the core architectural purpose of Insert & Find: Comparison & Logical Operators in the modern full-stack MERN ecosystem?",hi:"Modern full-stack MERN ecosystem mein Insert & Find: Operators ($gt, $in, $and, $or) ka mukhya architectural maksad kya hota hai?"},options:[{en:"It manages physical computer cooling and power supply",hi:"Ye physical computer cooling aur power supply manage karta hai"},{en:"It provides structured, robust, and scalable patterns for handling insert & find: comparison & logical operators with high performance and maintainability",hi:"Ye high performance aur maintainability ke saath Insert & Find: Operators ($gt, $in, $and, $or) ko handle karne ka structured aur scalable pattern provide karta hai"},{en:"It completely replaces JavaScript with binary machine code in browser tabs",hi:"Ye browser tabs mein JavaScript ko binary machine code se replace karta hai"},{en:"It is only used for printing documents to physical printers",hi:"Ye sirf physical printers par documents print karne ke liye hai"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Insert & Find: Comparison & Logical Operators establishes clean separation of concerns, ensuring predictable data flow, robust error handling, and optimal runtime performance in production.",hi:"Insert & Find: Operators ($gt, $in, $and, $or) clean architecture aur separation of concerns deta hai jisse application scalable aur maintainable banti hai."}},{question:{en:"What critical development bottleneck or anti-pattern does Insert & Find: Comparison & Logical Operators directly resolve?",hi:"Insert & Find: Operators ($gt, $in, $and, $or) kis critical development bottleneck ya anti-pattern ko seedhe solve karta hai?"},options:[{en:"It replaces chaotic, tightly coupled ad-hoc logic with declarative, predictable control flow and structured data contracts",hi:"Ye chaotic aur tightly coupled logic ko hata kar declarative, predictable flow aur structured data contracts deta hai"},{en:"It forces the operating system to shut down when errors occur",hi:"Error aane par ye operating system band kar deta hai"},{en:"It deletes all database records older than 24 hours automatically",hi:"Ye 24 ghante purane DB records delete karta hai"},{en:"It blocks all outgoing HTTP network requests to conserve bandwidth",hi:"Ye bandwidth bachane ke liye network requests block karta hai"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Without Insert & Find: Comparison & Logical Operators, applications suffer from brittle code, maintenance overhead, and unhandled edge cases that manifest as production crashes.",hi:"Insert & Find: Operators ($gt, $in, $and, $or) ke bina code brittle ho jata hai aur production mein unexpected errors aate hain."}},{question:{en:"When reasoning about Insert & Find: Comparison & Logical Operators, how is its mental model best conceptualized through real-world analogies?",hi:"Insert & Find: Operators ($gt, $in, $and, $or) ko real-world analogies ke zariye kaise best samjha ja sakta hai?"},options:[{en:"As a completely offline computer with zero network or database connections",hi:"Ek offline computer ki tarah jisme koi connection na ho"},{en:"As a disciplined, coordinated workflow where inputs are validated and processed through standardized checkpoints rather than ad-hoc handling",hi:"Ek disciplined workflow ki tarah jahan data ko structured checkpoints ke zariye step-by-step process kiya jata hai"},{en:"As a random number generator with non-deterministic output",hi:"Random number generator ki tarah jiska koi niyam na ho"},{en:"As a static text document that cannot be modified or read",hi:"Static text document jo padha na ja sake"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Real-world workflow analogies help engineers visualize component boundaries, request lifecycles, and data transformations intuitively.",hi:"Real-world analogies component boundaries aur request lifecycle ko visual aur intuitive banati hain."}},{question:{en:"When declaring and implementing Insert & Find: Comparison & Logical Operators, what syntactic convention is essential to prevent runtime errors?",hi:"Insert & Find: Operators ($gt, $in, $and, $or) ko declare aur implement karte waqt kaunsa syntax niyam runtime errors rokne ke liye zaroori hai?"},options:[{en:"Adhering strictly to required parameters, handling asynchronous promises/callbacks cleanly, and verifying return value types",hi:"Zaroori parameters sahi pass karna, async promises ko handle karna aur return value types verify karna"},{en:"Wrapping every line of code inside an eval() execution block",hi:"Har line ko eval() block mein wrap karna"},{en:"Omitting import and require statements to reduce file size",hi:"File size ghatane ke liye import statements hatana"},{en:"Writing all code on a single continuous line without whitespace",hi:"Bina whitespace ke single line par code likhna"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Following standard ES6+ syntax contracts and properly handling promise resolution ensures execution safety and eliminates TypeError exceptions.",hi:"ES6+ syntax aur promise handling ke standard rules follow karne se TypeError aur crashes nahi aate."}},{question:{en:"What is a common pitfall developers encounter when working with Insert & Find: Comparison & Logical Operators?",hi:"Insert & Find: Operators ($gt, $in, $and, $or) ke saath kaam karte waqt developers aksar kaunsi aam galati karte hain?"},options:[{en:"Writing unit tests before implementing features",hi:"Feature likhne se pehle unit tests likhna"},{en:"Failing to handle failure edge cases, mutating shared state directly, or neglecting defensive validation guard clauses",hi:"Failure edge cases ko handle na karna, shared state direct mutate karna ya validation guard clauses na lagana"},{en:"Using strict equality checks (===) instead of loose equality (==)",hi:"Loose equality ke badle strict equality use karna"},{en:"Writing clear inline code documentation",hi:"Clear inline code comments likhna"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Neglecting edge cases and error handling causes silent regressions and race conditions that surface under concurrent user workloads.",hi:"Edge cases aur error handling miss karne se high-traffic production load mein silent bugs paida hote hain."}},{question:{en:"According to production best practices, how should Insert & Find: Comparison & Logical Operators be architected for enterprise-grade stability?",hi:"Production best practices ke mutabiq enterprise-grade stability ke liye Insert & Find: Operators ($gt, $in, $and, $or) ko kaise architect karna chahiye?"},options:[{en:"Enforce modular boundaries, validate all incoming payloads against schemas, log structured context, and maintain pure functions where possible",hi:"Modular boundaries enforce karein, payloads ko schema se validate karein, structured logs rakhein aur pure functions use karein"},{en:"Hardcode sensitive database connection strings directly in client-side files",hi:"Database passwords ko client files mein hardcode karna"},{en:"Disable all linter rules and type warnings globally",hi:"Linter aur type warnings ko globally disable karna"},{en:"Store all user session variables in global un-scoped memory arrays",hi:"Global memory arrays mein sessions store karna"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Enterprise-grade code prioritizes modularity, strict input validation, structured observability, and stateless designs.",hi:"Production hardening ke liye modular code, schema validation aur observability standard rules hote hain."}},{question:{en:"How does proper optimization of Insert & Find: Comparison & Logical Operators impact application memory and CPU consumption?",hi:"Insert & Find: Operators ($gt, $in, $and, $or) ko sahi dhang se optimize karne par application memory aur CPU par kya asar padta hai?"},options:[{en:"It increases server CPU temperature to 100 degrees Celsius",hi:"Server CPU temperature 100 degrees kar deta hai"},{en:"It minimizes redundant computations, eliminates memory leaks from uncleaned references, and maintains low latency under high concurrency",hi:"Ye redundant computations ghatata hai, memory leaks khatam karta hai aur high concurrency mein low latency maintain karta hai"},{en:"It doubles heap RAM allocation unconditionally",hi:"Heap RAM ko zabardasti double karta hai"},{en:"Optimization has zero measurable impact in modern web engines",hi:"Modern web engines par optimization ka koi asar nahi hota"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Preventing unnecessary allocations and cleaning up resources ensures low garbage collection pressure and predictable response times.",hi:"Memory leak rokne aur unnecessary allocations hatane se Garbage Collector par load kam rehta hai aur response fast rehta hai."}},{question:{en:"What security principle is non-negotiable when handling data within Insert & Find: Comparison & Logical Operators?",hi:"Insert & Find: Operators ($gt, $in, $and, $or) mein data handle karte waqt kaunsa security principle non-negotiable hota hai?"},options:[{en:"Never trust client-supplied input: always sanitize, authenticate, authorize, and validate against strict schemas on the server",hi:"Client data par blind trust na karein: server par hamesha sanitize, authenticate, authorize aur validate karein"},{en:"Trust all requests coming from mobile devices or web browsers blindly",hi:"Mobile ya browser se aane wali requests par blind trust karein"},{en:"Disable HTTPS and SSL certificates to maximize raw network throughput",hi:"Network throughput ke liye HTTPS band karein"},{en:"Expose database admin credentials to all registered users",hi:"Database admin credentials sabhi users ko expose karein"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Zero-Trust security dictates that every incoming request and data mutation must be validated and authenticated server-side before processing.",hi:"Zero-Trust security ke mutabiq har incoming mutation ko server par strictly validate aur authenticate kiya jana chahiye."}},{question:{en:"How does asynchronous non-blocking execution operate in Insert & Find: Comparison & Logical Operators?",hi:"Insert & Find: Operators ($gt, $in, $and, $or) mein asynchronous non-blocking execution kaise kaam karta hai?"},options:[{en:"It freezes the entire operating system until each operation completes",hi:"Har operation complete hone tak operating system freeze rehta hai"},{en:"I/O operations return Promises or accept callbacks, delegating work to background threads/queues while the main thread remains free to handle incoming tasks",hi:"I/O operations Promises return karte hain aur background queues use karke main thread ko baaki requests ke liye free rakhte hain"},{en:"Async operations execute in reverse alphabetical order automatically",hi:"Async operations reverse alphabetical order mein chalte hain"},{en:"Async code only executes when triggered manually by a user click",hi:"Sirf manual user click par async code chalta hai"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Non-blocking asynchronous operations resolve via microtasks or event loop queues, ensuring the runtime thread serves concurrent requests smoothly.",hi:"Non-blocking model main thread ko free rakhta hai taaki server bina rukaawat ke multiple users ko simultaneously serve kar sake."}},{question:{en:"What is the recommended pattern for propagating errors that occur in Insert & Find: Comparison & Logical Operators?",hi:"Insert & Find: Operators ($gt, $in, $and, $or) mein error aane par unhe propagate karne ka recommended pattern kya hai?"},options:[{en:"Intercepting the error, enriching it with operational context, and delegating to a centralized error handler or error boundary",hi:"Error ko intercept karna, debug context add karna, aur centralized error handler ya error boundary ko pass karna"},{en:"Swallowing errors silently with empty catch {} blocks to hide problems from logs",hi:"Khaali catch {} blocks se errors ko silently daba dena taaki logs mein na dikhein"},{en:"Shutting down the server machine power immediately",hi:"Server machine power turant band kar dena"},{en:"Sending internal raw stack traces and database credentials to end-user browsers",hi:"Raw stack trace aur DB passwords browser par bhej dena"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Centralized error propagation provides complete operational observability while shielding internal infrastructure details from end users.",hi:"Centralized error handling se system mein transparency rehti hai aur user ko clean, safe error messages milte hain."}},{question:{en:"When authoring unit or integration tests for Insert & Find: Comparison & Logical Operators, what must the test suite assert?",hi:"Insert & Find: Operators ($gt, $in, $and, $or) ke liye automated tests likhte waqt test suite ko kya assert karna zaroori hai?"},options:[{en:"Only that the JavaScript file can be saved to disk",hi:"Sirf ye ki file disk par save ho sake"},{en:"Both the happy path (expected inputs producing valid outputs) AND boundary edge cases (null, empty arrays, network timeouts, invalid types)",hi:"Happy path (valid data) AUR boundary edge cases (null, empty array, network timeout, invalid types) dono ko verify karna"},{en:"That the test suite takes at least 24 hours to finish running",hi:"Test suite ko 24 ghante chalna chahiye"},{en:"Testing is considered unnecessary in modern full-stack development",hi:"Modern development mein testing zaroori nahi hai"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Robust automated test suites verify both standard valid scenarios and defensive failure modes to prevent regressions during deployments.",hi:"Achhi testing valid inputs aur failure states dono ko assert karti hai taaki production deployments safe rahein."}},{question:{en:"How does modular design enhance code maintainability in Insert & Find: Comparison & Logical Operators?",hi:"Modular design Insert & Find: Operators ($gt, $in, $and, $or) mein code maintainability ko kaise badhata hai?"},options:[{en:"By isolating distinct responsibilities into small, reusable, and independently testable units following the Single Responsibility Principle",hi:"Single Responsibility Principle ke zariye alag-alag kaamo ko chote, reusable aur testable units mein baant kar"},{en:"By combining all frontend, backend, and database code into a single 50,000-line script",hi:"Saara code ek hi 50,000-line script mein daal kar"},{en:"By removing all function names and replacing them with random numbers",hi:"Function names hata kar random numbers likhna"},{en:"By forbidding code comments and documentation across the repository",hi:"Comments aur documentation ban kar dena"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Modularity reduces cognitive load, simplifies debugging, prevents ripple effects during changes, and enables seamless team collaboration.",hi:"Modular code se readability badhti hai, debugging aasan hoti hai aur ek jagah badlav karne par doosri jagah bugs nahi aate."}},{question:{en:"When application traffic scales 100x, how should Insert & Find: Comparison & Logical Operators be architected to support horizontal scaling?",hi:"Traffic 100x badhne par Insert & Find: Operators ($gt, $in, $and, $or) ko horizontally scale karne ke liye kya design approach honi chahiye?"},options:[{en:"Ensure the component/service is completely stateless, offload shared session/state to Redis/MongoDB, and distribute traffic via a load balancer",hi:"Service ko completely stateless banayein, shared state ko Redis/DB par shift karein aur load balancer se traffic distribute karein"},{en:"Store all user session variables in local in-memory JavaScript objects on the web server",hi:"Server ki local RAM mein session variables store karna"},{en:"Reboot the production server manually whenever memory usage exceeds 10%",hi:"Memory 10% cross hote hi server manually reboot karna"},{en:"Block 95% of incoming users using firewall rules",hi:"95% users ko firewall se block kar dena"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Stateless service architecture guarantees that any container instance can handle any incoming request, enabling dynamic auto-scaling without session loss.",hi:"Stateless architecture auto-scaling ka base hai jahan naye containers bina session loss ke instant traffic handle kar sakte hain."}},{question:{en:"In the full-stack MERN paradigm, where does Insert & Find: Comparison & Logical Operators properly belong and execute?",hi:"Full-stack MERN architecture mein Insert & Find: Operators ($gt, $in, $and, $or) kahan belong karta hai aur kahan execute hota hai?"},options:[{en:"In its designated architectural tier (Client browser UI, Express API backend, or MongoDB database) with clean API contracts connecting them",hi:"Apne designated tier (Browser UI, Express API backend, ya MongoDB) mein clean API contracts ke saath"},{en:"Directly on the end-user's local router firmware",hi:"User ke local router firmware par"},{en:"Inside the computer motherboard BIOS chip",hi:"Motherboard BIOS chip mein"},{en:"All MERN code runs strictly inside the MongoDB database engine",hi:"Saara MERN code sirf MongoDB ke andar chalta hai"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Maintaining clear structural boundaries between client rendering, backend orchestration, and database persistence is the defining trait of MERN.",hi:"Client UI, backend server aur database ke beech saaf boundary maintain karna MERN architecture ka mukhya niyam hai."}},{question:{en:"What telemetry metric or observability signal is most crucial for diagnosing issues with Insert & Find: Comparison & Logical Operators in production?",hi:"Production mein Insert & Find: Operators ($gt, $in, $and, $or) ki problems diagnose karne ke liye sabse zaroori telemetry metric kaunsi hoti hai?"},options:[{en:"The desktop monitor brightness setting of the client",hi:"Client ke monitor ki brightness"},{en:"Latency percentiles (p95/p99), error rates (HTTP 4xx/5xx), throughput (RPS), and heap memory allocation deltas",hi:"Latency percentiles (p95/p99), error rates (4xx/5xx), throughput (RPS), aur heap memory allocation deltas"},{en:"The number of files in the project's root folder",hi:"Root folder mein files ki sankhya"},{en:"The physical keyboard model used by the engineer",hi:"Engineer ke keyboard ka model"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Observability platforms monitor p95/p99 latencies, error frequencies, and memory utilization to identify bottlenecks and regressions early.",hi:"p95/p99 latencies aur error rates monitor karne se crashes aane se pehle hi bottlenecks pakad mein aa jaate hain."}},{question:{en:"Why is eliminating unintended side effects essential when authoring logic for Insert & Find: Comparison & Logical Operators?",hi:"Insert & Find: Operators ($gt, $in, $and, $or) ka logic likhte waqt unintended side effects ko khatam karna kyun zaroori hai?"},options:[{en:"Side effects introduce unpredictability, corrupt shared state, cause race conditions, and make concurrent code nearly impossible to debug",hi:"Side effects se code unpredictable banta hai, shared state corrupt hoti hai aur race conditions create hoti hain"},{en:"Side effects permanently erase the developer's Git commit history",hi:"Git history permanently delete ho jaati hai"},{en:"Side effects are strictly required by the JavaScript ECMAScript standard",hi:"ECMAScript mein side effects required hain"},{en:"Side effects make all algorithms execute in O(1) time",hi:"Saare algorithms O(1) time mein chalte hain"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Pure and predictable logic produces the same output for identical inputs, guaranteeing thread safety, easy caching, and high reliability.",hi:"Pure logic se shared state safe rehti hai aur same input par hamesha consistent aur predictable output milta hai."}},{question:{en:"How should client-side state be kept in sync with backend server mutations in Insert & Find: Comparison & Logical Operators?",hi:"Insert & Find: Operators ($gt, $in, $and, $or) mein client-side state aur backend server data ko sync mein kaise rakha jata hai?"},options:[{en:"By forcing a complete hard page refresh every 3 seconds",hi:"Har 3 second mein poora page hard refresh karke"},{en:"Using optimistic UI updates with error rollback, automated query cache invalidation (TanStack Query/RTK), or WebSocket change streams",hi:"Optimistic UI updates with rollback, automated query cache invalidation ya WebSocket push streams use karke"},{en:"By disabling all database update operations permanently",hi:"Database updates ko permanently band karke"},{en:"By saving user state in local CSV files on the server desktop",hi:"Server desktop par CSV files save karke"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Modern full-stack architectures synchronize state seamlessly using query cache invalidation, optimistic updates, and real-time socket events.",hi:"Modern apps cache invalidation aur optimistic UI use karti hain taaki UI bina screen reload ke instantly updated rahe."}}]};export{e as default};
